    "global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10580",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In an experiment involving the toss of two dice, what is the probability that the sum is 6 or 7?\n\nOptions: \nA. 5/36\nB. 3/12\nC. 6/36\nD. 1/6\nE. 17/36\nF. 7/36\nG. 13/36\nH. 8/36\nI. 10/36\nJ. 11/36\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "glm-4-air",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "\\boxed{E}\n\nThe probability of rolling a sum of 6 with two dice can be calculated by considering the pairs (1,5), (2,4), (3,3), (4,2), and (5,1), which totals 5 different outcomes. The probability of rolling a sum of 7 can be found by considering the pairs (1,6), (2,5), (3,4), (4,3), (5,2), and (6,1), which totals 6 different outcomes. Since each die has 6 faces, there are \\(6 \\times 6 = 36\\) possible outcomes when rolling two dice. Thus, the probability of rolling a sum of 6 or 7 is \\(5 + 6 = 11\\) successful outcomes out of 36, which simplifies to \\(11/36\\).",
