    "global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10770",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Using the definition of the unilateral Z transform, F (z) = ^\\infty\\sum_n=0 f[n] z^-n. find the z - transform of the step-sequence f[n] = u[n].\n\nOptions: \nA. [1 / (z - 1)]\nB. [z / (1 + z)]\nC. [z^2 / (z - 1)]\nD. [1 / (2 - z)]\nE. [(z - 1) / z]\nF. [1 / (z^2 - 1)]\nG. [1 / (1 - z)]\nH. [z / (1 - z)]\nI. [z / (z - 1)]\nJ. [z / (z^2 - 1)]\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "glm-4-air",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "\\boxed{G}\n\nThe unilateral Z transform of the unit step sequence \\( u[n] \\), which is defined as \\( u[n] = 1 \\) for \\( n \\geq 0 \\), is \\( \\frac{1}{1 - z^{-1}} \\). Multiplying both numerator and denominator by \\( z \\) to get rid of the negative exponent gives us \\( \\frac{z}{z - 1} \\), which corresponds to option G.",
