  {
    "global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10561",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Compute the conditional distribution of Y given X if X and Y are jointly distributed with density f(x, y) = x + y0 < x < 1, 0 < y < 1 and = 0otherwise. What is the conditional expectation of Y?\n\nOptions: \nA. (x + 2) / {{2(x + 1)}}\nB. (2x + 3) / {{2(3x + 1)}}\nC. (2x + 2) / {{4(2x + 1)}}\nD. (3x + 3) / {{3(3x + 2)}}\nE. (2x + 1) / {{3(x + 2)}}\nF. (x + 1) / {{2(2x + 1)}}\nG. (3x + 2) / {{3(2x + 1)}}\nH. (3x + 1) / {{3(2x + 2)}}\nI. (4x + 2) / {{4(3x + 1)}}\nJ. (3x + 2) / {{4(2x + 1)}}\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "glm-4-air",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The conditional distribution of Y given X can be found by computing the conditional density function \\( f_{Y|X}(y|x) \\) which is given by \\( \\frac{f(x, y)}{f_X(x)} \\). The marginal density function \\( f_X(x) \\) is found by integrating \\( f(x, y) \\) over y, resulting in \\( f_X(x) = \\int_{0}^{1} (x + y) dy = x + \\frac{1}{2} \\). Thus, the conditional density function is \\( f_{Y|X}(y|x) = \\frac{x + y}{x + \\frac{1}{2}} \\). The conditional expectation \\( E(Y|X) \\) is calculated by integrating y times the conditional density function over the range of y. After integrating and simplifying, the correct choice is \\boxed{F}. The conditional expectation of Y given X is \\( \\frac{x + 1}{2(2x + 1)} \\).",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
        "input_tokens": 311,
        "output_tokens": 213,
        "total_tokens": 524
      },
