    "prediction": "glm-4-air",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The entropy \\( H \\) of a set of messages can be calculated using the formula:\n\n\\[\nH = -\\sum_{i=1}^{n} P(x_i) \\log_2 P(x_i)\n\\]\n\nFor the given probabilities, the entropy is:\n\n\\[\nH = -( \\frac{1}{4} \\log_2 \\frac{1}{4} + \\frac{1}{4} \\log_2 \\frac{1}{4} + \\frac{1}{8} \\log_2 \\frac{1}{8} + \\frac{1}{8} \\log_2 \\frac{1}{8} + \\frac{1}{8} \\log_2 \\frac{1}{8} + \\frac{1}{8} \\log_2 \\frac{1}{8} )\n\\]\n\n\\[\nH = -( 2 \\times \\frac{1}{4} + 4 \\times \\frac{1}{8} )\n\\]\n\n\\[\nH = -( 0.5 + 0.5 )\n\\]\n\n\\[\nH = -1 = 1 \\text{ bit/message}\n\\]\n\nHowever, there seems to be a miscalculation in the simplification process. Let's correct that:\n\n\\[\nH = -\\left( 2 \\times \\frac{1}{4} \\log_2 \\frac{1}{4} + 4 \\times \\frac{1}{8} \\log_2 \\frac{1}{8} \\right)\n\\]\n\\[\nH = -\\left( 2 \\times \\frac{1}{4} \\times 2 + 4 \\times \\frac{1}{8} \\times 3 \\right)\n\\]\n\\[\nH = -( 1 + 1.5 )\n\\]\n\\[\nH = -2.5 = 2.5 \\text{ bits/message}\n\\]\n\nThus, the correct answer is \\boxed{I}.",
