    "global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10759",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A gravity fed lock in a proposed shipping canal is to be studied with a 1/100-scale geometrically similar model. (a) If the model lock fills in 0.8 min, estimate the time for the prototype to fill. (b) Find the ratio of corresponding mass flow rates in the model and prototype locks.\n\nOptions: \nA. 5 min, \\(\\lambda^7/2\\)\nB. 9 min, \\lambda^3/2\nC. 11 min, \\(\\lambda^4\\)\nD. 12 min, \\(\\lambda^5/3\\)\nE. 7 min, \\lambda^4/2\nF. 6 min, \\lambda^6/2\nG. 8 min, \\lambda^5/2\nH. 4 min, \\(\\lambda^2\\)\nI. 10 min, \\(\\lambda^3\\)\nJ. 15 min, \\(\\lambda^7/3\\)\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "glm-4-air",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The time ratio for filling the lock can be found using the scale ratio raised to the power of the dimensionless exponent for time in the Froude similarity, which for filling time is typically \\( \\lambda^{2/3} \\) since filling time is proportional to the square root of the length of the lock divided by the square root of the acceleration due to gravity. Given the model lock fills in 0.8 minutes and the scale ratio (\\( \\lambda \\)) is 100, the prototype time (\\( T_p \\)) can be estimated as \\( T_p = T_m \\cdot \\lambda^{2/3} \\). Plugging in the numbers, we get \\( T_p = 0.8 \\times 100^{2/3} \\) which calculates to approximately 8 minutes. The corresponding mass flow rate ratio is \\( \\lambda^3 \\) due to the similarity of flow rates in geometrically similar systems under dynamic similarity. Thus, the correct choice is \\boxed{G} (8 min, \\( \\lambda^5/2 \\)), but note that the mass flow rate part of the option is incorrect, as it should be \\( \\lambda^3 \\), not \\( \\lambda^5/2 \\).",
