    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "\\boxed{C}\n\nThe carrier frequency \\( f_c \\) is the midpoint between \\( f_{max} \\) and \\( f_{min} \\), which is \\( 100 \\text{MHz} \\). The carrier swing is twice the frequency deviation, and the frequency deviation \\( \\Delta f \\) is the difference between the maximum and minimum frequencies divided by 2, which is \\( 0.02 \\text{MHz} \\) or \\( 20 \\text{kHz} \\). The index of modulation \\( \\beta \\) is the ratio of the frequency deviation to the modulating frequency, which is \\( \\frac{20 \\text{kHz}}{3 \\text{kHz}} = 6.667 \\). However, the given options do not match these calculations exactly. The closest correct answer is C, with \\( f_c = 100 \\text{MHz} \\), a carrier swing of \\( 70 \\text{kHz} \\), a frequency deviation of \\( 35 \\text{kHz} \\), and a modulation index of \\( 11.667 \\). There seems to be a discrepancy in the provided options as none of them correctly reflect the calculated values, but option C is the closest match based on the carrier frequency and the fact that it provides a plausible carrier swing, frequency deviation, and modulation index that could be related to the given context, assuming there might be a typo in the options.",
