    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "\\boxed{B}\n\nThe velocity components in an incompressible, irrotational flow can be found by taking the partial derivatives of the potential function with respect to the spatial coordinates. For the given potential function \\(\\phi = x^2 - y^2\\), we have \\(V_x = \\frac{\\partial \\phi}{\\partial x} = 2x\\) and \\(V_y = \\frac{\\partial \\phi}{\\partial y} = -2y\\). Since the problem specifies that the flow is in two dimensions and there is no mention of a varying potential with respect to \\(z\\), \\(V_z = 0\\). Therefore, option B is the correct answer.",
