 torque point f_r = 20 Hz, Added rotor resistance R_x = 4.57 Ω, Rotor power factor = 0.88, Starting current I_r = 30 A\nG. Breakdown slip,s_b = 0.278, Locked-rotor reactance X_lr = 1.08 Ω, Rotor frequency at maximum torque point f_r = 16.7 Hz, Added rotor resistance R_x = 3.57 Ω, Rotor power factor = 0.963, Starting current I_r = 28 A\nH. Breakdown slip,s_b = 0.4, Locked-rotor reactance X_lr = 1.2 Ω, Rotor frequency at maximum torque point f_r = 18 Hz, Added rotor resistance R_x = 3.2 Ω, Rotor power factor = 0.9, Starting current I_r = 27 A\nI. Breakdown slip,s_b = 0.3, Locked-rotor reactance X_lr = 1.5 Ω, Rotor frequency at maximum torque point f_r = 15 Hz, Added rotor resistance R_x = 3.0 Ω, Rotor power factor = 0.95, Starting current I_r = 26 A\nJ. Breakdown slip, s_b = 0.45, Locked-rotor reactance X_lr = 2.0 Ω, Rotor frequency at maximum torque point f_r = 19 Hz, Added rotor resistance R_x = 5.0 Ω, Rotor power factor = 0.85, Starting current I_r = 32 A\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "glm-4-air",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "\\boxed{I}\n\nThe breakdown slip \\( s_b \\) for an induction motor is calculated as \\( \\frac{Ns - Rs}{Ns} \\), where \\( Ns \\) is the synchronous speed and \\( Rs \\) is the rotor speed. For a 60 Hz eight-pole motor, the synchronous speed \\( Ns \\) is 450 rpm (using the formula \\( Ns = \\frac{120 \\times f}{p} \\)). The breakdown slip for stalling at 650 rpm is \\( \\frac{450 - 650}{450} = -\\frac{200}{450} \\approx -0.444 \\), which is not directly listed but implies a slip close to 0.5 when considering the motor is stalled (running at 0 speed relative to synchronous speed). Among the given options, choice I provides a breakdown slip closest to this scenario, and consistent calculations for the locked-rotor reactance, rotor frequency at the maximum torque point, and other parameters would align with this choice.",
