      "generated_answer": "\\boxed{G}\n\nThe most accurate rationale for questioning the validity of the efficacy analysis among African American study subjects is that vaccine response among African American subjects was not the primary outcome measure. Post hoc analyses, like the one described, are exploratory and not as reliable as pre-specified analyses because they are more susceptible to Type I errors (false positives) due to multiple comparisons. The primary endpoint of the study was the overall benefit of the vaccine, not its efficacy within specific subgroups.",
