    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In a cohort study of elderly women, the relative risk ratio for hip fractures among those who exercise regularly is 1.2 (95% confidence interval of 1.1 to 1.8). Which of the following is the most appropriate conclusion about the effect of regular exercise on the risk for hip fracture?\n\nOptions: \nA. Statistically significant overall increase in risk\nB. Statistically insignificant change in risk for those who exercise regularly\nC. Statistically significant overall decrease in risk\nD. Statistically nonsignificant decrease in risk\nE. Statistically significant decrease in risk only for those over 80\nF. Statistically significant overall decrease in risk for those who exercise regularly\nG. Statistically nonsignificant overall decrease in risk\nH. Statistically significant increase in risk only for those under 70\nI. No statistically significant change in risk\nJ. Statistically nonsignificant increase in risk\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
