    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "\\boxed{D}\n\nThe Angiotensin 1 receptor (AT1 receptor) typically activates Gq/11 proteins leading to phospholipase C (PLC) activation and subsequent production of inositol triphosphate (IP3) and diacylglycerol (DAG), which lead to calcium release and protein kinase C activation. It is not known to act through the opening of potassium channels. In contrast, Muscarinic M2, Dopamine D2, and Serotonin 5 HT1 receptors are associated with the opening of potassium channels through Gi/o protein activation, which leads to hyperpolarization of the cell membrane.",
