    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "\\boxed{B}\n\nIn uncontrolled diabetes mellitus, there is typically an increased activity of hormone-sensitive lipase (HSL) due to insulin resistance, leading to increased lipolysis and free fatty acids in the bloodstream. These elevated free fatty acids are taken up by the liver and contribute to the increased synthesis of triglycerides and very low-density lipoproteins (VLDL). Additionally, decreased activity of lipoprotein lipase (LPL) can contribute to elevated triglycerides because LPL is necessary for the breakdown of triglycerides in lipoproteins.",
