    "prediction": "glm-4-air",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "\\boxed{C}\n\nIn Neo-Riemannian theory, the N relation (Nebenverwandt) involves applying the R (raise bass by a step), L (lower bass by a step), and P (raise root by a step) transformations to a triad. Starting with a C major triad (C-E-G), applying R gives us an E minor triad (E-G-B), applying L gives us an A minor triad (A-C-E), and applying P gives us a G major triad (G-B-D). However, the combination of these transformations leads to the f minor triad (F-A-C), as raising the root of C major by a step (P) gives us D major, then lowering the bass (L) from D major gives us B minor, and finally raising the bass (R) from B minor gives us f minor.",
