    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "\\boxed{F Major}\n\nThe pattern of expanding intervals in alternating directions can be observed as follows: from B-flat to C is a minor third (upward), C to A is a minor third (downward), A to D is a perfect fourth (upward), D to G is a perfect fifth (downward), G to E is a major third (upward), and E to the next tonic (which we are deducing) should be a minor sixth (downward). The minor sixth from E down is F, thus deducing the key of the seventh piece to be F Major.",
