    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The king imposes a trial in which the accused must choose between two doors: one leading to a hungry tiger that will kill them if opened, and the other leading to a suitable lady with whom they will immediately marry if opened. This trial is meant to determine innocence or guilt by chance. The accused has no guidance or influence other than the impartial and incorruptible chance provided by this choice. \n\n\\boxed{{a trial by choosing between two doors, one with a tiger and the other with a lady}}",
