      "generated_answer": "\\boxed{C}\n\nThe Carlsbad Resolutions were aimed at suppressing nationalist revolutions across the continent. Metternich, as a leading figure in the Congress of Vienna, sought to maintain the status quo and stability of the post-Napoleonic era, which included suppressing nationalist movements that could threaten the existing order. Thus, option C is the most accurate reflection of Metternich's intent with these resolutions.",
      "success": true,
