      "generated_answer": "\\boxed{C}\n\nThe instruction to remain nonviolent is most closely associated with the civil rights movements that changed the legal status of minorities in the United States, as these movements were heavily inspired by Mahatma Gandhi's philosophy of nonviolent resistance. Martin Luther King Jr., a key figure in the U.S. civil rights movement, was significantly influenced by Gandhi's strategies. The other options are related to different ideologies or struggles that did not primarily emphasize nonviolent methods.",
