      "generated_answer": "\\boxed{C}\n\nThe excerpt indicates that the Mongol administration in China allowed for a variety of religious communities to flourish, had a structured bureaucratic system, and was integrated into international trade and communication, which aligns with option C's description of a centralized Chinese bureaucratic state. Meanwhile, the Mongol administration in Russia is known to have relied heavily on tribute from the principalities, fitting option C's description of the difference in administration styles.",
