    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "\\boxed{C}\n\nThe Inca Empire was indeed weakened by a civil war at the time Francisco Pizarro arrived, which made it easier for the Spanish to conquer them. This internal strife, combined with factors such as Pizarro's superior military technology and psychological tactics, contributed to the Inca's defeat. None of the options perfectly encapsulate all the reasons, but option C is the most accurate single factor among those given.",
