      "generated_answer": "\\boxed{F}\n\nKipling's poem refers to the \"White Man's Burden\" as a difficult duty that requires patience and perseverance, indicating that it is a task that is challenging but necessary. The phrase \"bind your sons to exile\" and \"wait in heavy harness\" implies a burdensome and arduous endeavor, which aligns with option F. Other options, while somewhat reflective of the poem's themes, do not encapsulate the notion of difficulty and necessity as directly as option F does.",
