    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "\\boxed{C}\n\nProblems often arise when archaeologists are not culturally sensitive to the spiritual beliefs of the Native Americans, as this can lead to conflicts over the handling and repatriation of human remains and cultural items. The Native American Graves Protection and Repatriation Act (NAGPRA) specifically addresses these ethical concerns. Other options, while potentially problematic, do not directly address the core ethical issues that NAGPRA is designed to resolve.",
